text-primary\",\"children\":[\"51.10\",\"%\"]}],[\"$\",\"$L4c\",null,{\"k\":\"pages.heroes.rankSentenceMid1\",\"params\":{\"name\":\"Freya\",\"delta\":\"+3.02%\"}}],[\"$\",\"strong\",null,{\"className\":\"text-text-primary\",\"children\":[\"0.80\",\"%\"]}],[\"$\",\"$L4c\",null,{\"k\":\"pages.heroes.rankSentenceMid2\"}],[\"$\",\"strong\",null,{\"className\":\"text-text-primary\",\"children\":[\"1.04\",\"%\"]}],[\"$\",\"$L4c\",null,{\"k\":\"pages.heroes.rankSentenceAfter\",\"params\":{\"rank\":\"Mythical Glory+\"}}]]}]]}]\na9:[\"$\",\"strong\",\"strong-1\",{\"className\":\"text-[#E8E6E3] font-semibold\",\"children\":\"Swift Boots\"}]\naa:[\"$\",\"p\",\"p-6\",{\"className\":\"text-[#9BA0B4] leading-relaxed mb-4 text-[15px]\",\"children\":[\"The weakest common default is \",[\"$\",\"strong\",\"strong-0\",{\"className\":\"text-[#E8E6E3] font-semibold\",\"children\":\"Blade of Despair\"}],\". It is the cargo-cult fighter item: +160 physical attack looks huge on paper, but Despair's passive only activates under 50% HP, which is the window Freya's enemies are usually already dead or disengaged. Build it fifth at earliest, and only if the game is over 20 minutes and you are ahead.\"]}]\nab:[\"$\",\"h2\",\"h2-1\",{\"className\":\"text-xl md:text-[26px] font-heading font-bold text-[#F0D060] mt-10 mb-4 first:mt-0 text-balance uppercase tracking-[0.04em] leading-tight relative\",\"children\":[[\"$\",\"span\",null,{\"aria-hidden\":\"true\",\"className\":\"block w-10 h-[3px] bg-gradient-to-r from-[#F0D060] to-[#C8AA6E]/0 mb-3\"}],\"Mistakes that lose Freya games\"]}]\nac:[\"$\",\"p\",\"p-7\",{\"className\":\"text-[#9BA0B4] leading-relaxed mb-4 text-[15px]\",\"children\":[[\"$\",\"strong\",\"strong-0\",{\"className\":\"text-[#E8E6E3] font-semibold\",\"children\":\"Ulting Phoveus because he has low HP.\"}],\" Every skill you cast near Phoveus reduces his cooldowns through Astaros' Gaze. Your S1 leap, your ult dive, even your S2 charge, all feed his CDR. When you ult him, you trigger his Infernal Pursuit counter-ult (Judgment), which smashes you for bonus damage scaled to your Max HP and heals him a slice of his missing health. The correct play against Phoveus is to \",[\"$\",\"strong\",\"strong-1\",{\"className\":\"text-[#E8E6E3] font-semibold\",\"children\":\"never initiate\"}],\". Let your tank engage, ult the enemy marksman instead, and ignore Phoveus entirely unless you have more than 50% HP advantage.\"]}]\nad:[\"$\",\"p\",\"p-8\",{\"className\":\"text-[#9BA0B4] leading-relaxed mb-4 text-[15px]\",\"children\":[[\"$\",\"strong\",\"strong-0\",{\"className\":\"text-[#E8E6E3] font-semibold\",\"children\":\"Engaging Minsitthar's ult zone.\"}],\" King's Calling prevents movement skills for enemies inside the field. Freya's S1 and S2 are both movement skills. Inside his ult, you have 0 escape, 0 engage, and 0 gap-close. If you see Minsitthar ult, walk sideways out of the zone before casting anything. If he ults on top of your ult landing spot, your 10-second Valkyrie state becomes 10 seconds of basic-attacking royal guards.\"]}]\nae:[\"$\",\"p\",\"p-9\",{\"className\":\"text-[#9BA0B4] leading-relaxed mb-4 text-[15px]\",\"children\":[[\"$\",\"strong\",\"strong-0\",{\"className\":\"text-[#E8E6E3] font-semibold\",\"children\":\"Spending all 6 orbs to clear a wave 10 seconds before a teamfight.\"}],\" The orb regen out of combat is slow. If you push a wave with 3 S2 casts (burning all 6 orbs) and your team engages at the Lord pit 10 seconds later, you arrive with an empty bar and no attack-speed empowerment. Keep 4 orbs in reserve whenever you see enemies missing on the minimap.\"]}]\naf:[\"$\",\"p\",\"p-10\",{\"className\":\"text-[#9BA0B4] leading-relaxed mb-4 text-[15px]\",\"children\":[[\"$\",\"strong\",\"strong-0\",{\"className\":\"text-[#E8E6E3] font-semibold\",\"children\":\"S1 as a dodge tool.\"}],\" The leap looks like Chou's Jump Kick or Hayabusa's Quad Shadow. It is not. It is an 8-second cooldown CC tool, not an evasion. Using it to avoid a Franco hook that is already airborne does nothing (the hook tracks through the leap). Using it to engage before your damage is stacked burns the cooldown and leaves you stuck in melee with no follow-up.\"]}]\nb0:[\"$\",\"p\",\"p-11\",{\"className\":\"text-[#9BA0B4] leading-relaxed mb-4 text-[15px]\",\"children\":[[\"$\",\"strong\",\"strong-0\",{\"className\":\"text-[#E8E6E3] font-semibold\",\"children\":\"Buying Retribution in EXP lane.\"}],\" The old community build pattern pushed Retribution for \\\"jungle flexibility.\\\" In the current patch, Freya is a 2-difficulty EXP/jungle hero with a clear lane identity. EXP Freya runs Flicker. Jungle Freya runs Retribution. Mixing them costs you the mode advantage of whichever lane you ended up in.\"]}]\nb1:[\"$\",\"h2\",\"h2-2\",{\"className\":\"text-xl md:text-[26px] font-heading font-bold text-[#F0D060] mt-10 mb-4 first:mt-0 text-balance uppercase tracking-[0.04em] leading-tight relative\",\"children\":[[\"$\",\"span\",null,{\"aria-hidden\":\"true\",\"className\":\"block w-10 h-[3px] bg-gradient-to-r from-[#F0D060] to-[#C8AA6E]/0 mb-3\"}],\"Key tips\"]}]\nb2:[\"$\",\"div\",\"blockquote-0\",{\"className\":\"my-5 p-4 flex gap-3\",\"style\":{\"background\":\"rgba(200,170,110,0.08)\",\"border\":\"1px solid rgba(200,170,110,0.35)\"},\"children\":[[\"$\",\"svg\",null,{\"ref\":\"$undefined\",\"xmlns\":\"http://www.w3.org/2000/svg\",\"width\":24,\"height\":24,\"viewBox\":\"0 0 24 24\",\"fill\":\"none\",\"stroke\":\"currentColor\",\"strokeWidth\":2,\"strokeLinecap\":\"round\",\"strokeLinejoin\":\"round\",\"className\":\"lucide lucide-lightbulb w-4 h-4 flex-shrink-0 mt-0.5\",\"aria-hidden\":\"true\",\"style\":{\"color\":\"#C8AA6E\"},\"children\":[[\"$\",\"path\",\"1gvzjb\",{\"d\":\"M15 14c.2-1 .7-1.7 1.5-2.5 1-.9 1.5-2.2 1.5-3.5A6 6 0 0 0 6 8c0 1 .2 2.2 1.5 3.5.7.7 1.3 1.5 1.5 2.5\"}],[\"$\",\"path\",\"x1upvd\",{\"d\":\"M9 18h6\"}],[\"$\",\"path\",\"ceow96\",{\"d\":\"M10 22h4\"}],\"$undefined\"]}],[\"$\",\"div\",null,{\"className\":\"min-w-0 flex-1\",\"children\":[[\"$\",\"p\",null,{\"className\":\"text-[11px] font-heading font-bold uppercase tracking-wider mb-1\",\"style\":{\"color\":\"#C8AA6E\"},\"children\":\"Tip\"}],[[\"$\",\"p\",\"0\",{\"className\":\"text-sm text-[#9BA0B4] leading-relaxed\",\"children\":[[\"$\",\"strong\",\".$strong-0\",{\"className\":\"text-[#E8E6E3] font-semibold\",\"children\":\"Fighter Emblem with Brave Smite core is non-negotiable.\"}],\" The Core talent heals 5% Max HP on skill damage with a 6-second cooldown. Freya casts damage-dealing skills every 2-3 seconds in a fight, so Brave Smite procs twice per Valkyrie window, partially replacing the HP regen the 2.1.61 patch took out of her ult.\"]}]]]}]]}]\nb3:[\"$\",\"div\",\"blockquote-1\",{\"className\":\"my-5 p-4 flex gap-3\",\"style\":{\"background\":\"rgba(0,170,255,0.08)\",\"border\":\"1px solid rgba(0,170,255,0.35)\"},\"children\":[[\"$\",\"svg\",null,{\"ref\":\"$undefined\",\"xmlns\":\"http://www.w3.org/2000/svg\",\"width\":24,\"height\":24,\"viewBox\":\"0 0 24 24\",\"fill\":\"none\",\"stroke\":\"currentColor\",\"strokeWidth\":2,\"strokeLinecap\":\"round\",\"strokeLinejoin\":\"round\",\"className\":\"lucide lucide-info w-4 h-4 flex-shrink-0 mt-0.5\",\"aria-hidden\":\"true\",\"style\":{\"color\":\"#00AAFF\"},\"children\":[[\"$\",\"circle\",\"1mglay\",{\"cx\":\"12\",\"cy\":\"12\",\"r\":\"10\"}],[\"$\",\"path\",\"1dtifu\",{\"d\":\"M12 16v-4\"}],[\"$\",\"path\",\"e9boi3\",{\"d\":\"M12 8h.01\"}],\"$undefined\"]}],[\"$\",\"div\",null,{\"className\":\"min-w-0 flex-1\",\"children\":[[\"$\",\"p\",null,{\"className\":\"text-[11px] font-heading font-bold uppercase tracking-wider mb-1\",\"style\":{\"color\":\"#00AAFF\"},\"children\":\"Note\"}],[[\"$\",\"p\",\"0\",{\"className\":\"text-sm text-[#9BA0B4] leading-relaxed\",\"children\":[[\"$\",\"strong\",\".$strong-0\",{\"className\":\"text-[#E8E6E3] font-semibold\",\"children\":\"Freya's ult is castable during animations other heroes cannot act through.\"}],\" You can cancel the end-lag of a basic attack by queuing ult instantly. This is roughly a 0.3-second cast-speed gain per fight opener and the single easiest mechanical improvement for new Freya players.\"]}]]]}]]}]\nb4:[\"$\",\"div\",\"blockquote-2\",{\"className\":\"my-5 p-4 flex gap-3\",\"style\":{\"background\":\"rgba(200,170,110,0.08)\",\"border\":\"1px solid rgba(200,170,110,0.35)\"},\"children\":[[\"$\",\"svg\",null,{\"ref\":\"$undefined\",\"xmlns\":\"http://www.w3.org/2000/svg\",\"width\":24,\"height\":24,\"viewBox\":\"0 0 24 24\",\"fill\":\"none\",\"stroke\":\"currentColor\",\"strokeWidth\":2,\"strokeLinecap\":\"round\",\"strokeLinejoin\":\"round\",\"className\":\"lucide lucide-lightbulb w-4 h-4 flex-shrink-0 mt-0.5\",\"aria-hidden\":\"true\",\"style\":{\"color\":\"#C8AA6E\"},\"children\":[[\"$\",\"path\",\"1gvzjb\",{\"d\":\"M15 14c.2-1 .7-1.7 1.5-2.5 1-.9 1.5-2.2 1.5-3.5A6 6 0 0 0 6 8c0 1 .2 2.2 1.5 3.5.7.7 1.3 1.5 1.5 2.5\"}],[\"$\",\"path\",\"x1upvd\",{\"d\":\"M9 18h6\"}],[\"$\",\"path\",\"ceow96\",{\"d\":\"M10 22h4\"}],\"$undefined\"]}],[\"$\",\"div\",null,{\"className\":\"min-w-0 flex-1\",\"children\":[[\"$\",\"p\",null,{\"className\":\"text-[11px] font-heading font-bold uppercase tracking-wider mb-1\",\"style\":{\"color\":\"#C8AA6E\"},\"children\":\"Tip\"}],[[\"$\",\"p\",\"0\",{\"className\":\"text-sm text-[#9BA0B4] leading-relaxed\",\"children\":[[\"$\",\"strong\",\".$strong-0\",{\"className\":\"text-[#E8E6E3] font-semibold\",\"children\":\"Her best matchups are heroes who need a full rotation to escape.\"}],\" Against Harith, Kagura, and Yve (all heroes with dash-dependent kits), the live matchup data is genuinely in her favor: you can S1 into them before they have blink charges stacked, and a full bar of empowered basics kills them before their dash is back.\"]}]]]}]]}]\nb5:[\"$\",\"div\",\"blockquote-3\",{\"className\":\"my-5 p-4 flex gap-3\",\"style\":{\"background\":\"rgba(255,107,107,0.08)\",\"border\":\"1px solid rgba(255,107,107,0.35)\"},\"children\":[[\"$\",\"svg\",null,{\"ref\":\"$undefined\",\"xmlns\":\"http://www.w3.org/2000/svg\",\"width\":24,\"height\":24,\"viewBox\":\"0 0 24 24\",\"fill\":\"none\",\"stroke\":\"currentColor\",\"strokeWidth\":2,\"strokeLinecap\":\"round\",\"strokeLinejoin\":\"round\",\"className\":\"lucide lucide-triangle-alert w-4 h-4 flex-shrink-0 mt-0.5\",\"aria-hidden\":\"true\",\"style\":{\"color\":\"#ff6b6b\"},\"children\":[[\"$\",\"path\",\"wmoenq\",{\"d\":\"m21.73 18-8-14a2 2 0 0 0-3.48 0l-8 14A2 2 0 0 0 4 21h16a2 2 0 0 0 1.73-3\"}],[\"$\",\"path\",\"juzpu7\",{\"d\":\"M12 9v4\"}],[\"$\",\"path\",\"p32p05\",{\"d\":\"M12 17h.01\"}],\"$undefined\"]}],[\"$\",\"div\",null,{\"className\":\"min-w-0 flex-1\",\"children\":[[\"$\",\"p\",null,{\"className\":\"text-[11px] font-heading font-bold uppercase tracking-wider mb-1\",\"style\":{\"color\":\"#ff6b6b\"},\"children\":\"Warning\"}],[[\"$\",\"p\",\"0\",{\"className\":\"text-sm text-[#9BA0B4] leading-relaxed\",\"children\":[[\"$\",\"strong\",\".$strong-0\",{\"className\":\"text-[#E8E6E3] font-semibold\",\"children\":\"Patch 2.1.88 cut the Valkyrie window from 12 to 10 seconds and raised the cooldown from 34-26s to 44-28s.\"}],\" You have less damage output per ult and a longer wait between windows. The sustain nerfs from 2.1.61 (HP regen 60-120 down to 40-80) are still in effect on top of this. Do not play Freya as a face-tank: commit only when you can reach the backline cleanly and exit before the window runs out.\"]}]]]}]]}]\nb6:[\"$\",\"div\",\"blockquote-4\",{\"className\":\"my-5 p-4 flex gap-3\",\"style\":{\"background\":\"rgba(0,170,255,0.08)\",\"border\":\"1px solid rgba(0,170,255,0.35)\"},\"children\":[[\"$\",\"svg\",null,{\"ref\":\"$undefined\",\"xmlns\":\"http://www.w3.org/2000/svg\",\"width\":24,\"height\":24,\"viewBox\":\"0 0 24 24\",\"fill\":\"none\",\"stroke\":\"currentColor\",\"strokeWidth\":2,\"strokeLinecap\":\"round\",\"strokeLinejoin\":\"round\",\"className\":\"lucide lucide-info w-4 h-4 flex-shrink-0 mt-0.5\",\"aria-hidden\":\"true\",\"style\":{\"color\":\"#00AAFF\"},\"children\":[[\"$\",\"circle\",\"1mglay\",{\"cx\":\"12\",\"cy\":\"12\",\"r\":\"10\"}],[\"$\",\"path\",\"1dtifu\",{\"d\":\"M12 16v-4\"}],[\"$\",\"path\",\"e9boi3\",{\"d\":\"M12 8h.01\"}],\"$undefined\"]}],[\"$\",\"div\",null,{\"className\":\"min-w-0 flex-1\",\"children\":[[\"$\",\"p\",null,{\"className\":\"text-[11px] font-heading font-bold uppercase tracking-wider mb-1\",\"style\":{\"color\":\"#00AAFF\"},\"children\":\"Note\"}],[[\"$\",\"p\",\"0\",{\"className\":\"text-sm text-[#9BA0B4] leading-relaxed\",\"children\":[[\"$\",\"strong\",\".$strong-0\",{\"className\":\"text-[#E8E6E3] font-semibold\",\"children\":\"The 3-2-1 skill order (Ultimate \u003e S2 \u003e S1) is correct for EXP lane, not jungle.\"}],\" In jungle, run 2-3-1 to keep clear speed through S2 orb dumps before your first ult unlocks. Check which role you are before locking in level-up order.\"]}]]]}]]}]\n"])</script></body></html>